date_type = 1
edits_description = "The image was cropped and the text was removed."
final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_x4myr")
province = 66
blurb = "Depicts two members of a hiking party crossing a stream below the Kirifuri (\"falling mist\") Waterfall, while others are taking in the view from the opposite side.

The Kirifuri Waterfall, still existing today, is located north of Nikkō City in present-day Tochigi prefecture, on the southeastern foothills of Mount Akanagi. The waterfall is over 75 meters high, and descends in three steps, first dropping vertically, then gliding almost horizontally, before again plunging and breaking into numerous writhing streams as it rushes over craggy rocks."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
